# Authored contribution practice; no actual submission, editorial decision or sharing.
Feature: Turn a workflow improvement into an explainable contribution

  Scenario: CONTRIB-001 — Propose a checkable change to an exact workflow
    Given an original invented workflow and a source with separately assigned tasks and dates
    When the learner identifies an unsupported deadline and proposes a revised check
    Then the proposal names the source version, observed problem and exact improvement
    And its evidence and limits remain distinguishable from a usefulness claim
    And its sources and rights note describes original invented material

  Scenario: CONTRIB-002 — Retain the first proposal while explaining a revision
    Given a first proposal and a supplied editorial comment about proposed dates
    When the learner writes a revision and a source-based reason
    Then the first proposal and new wording stay separately inspectable
    And a later edit clears the proposal self-check
    And the optional contribution does not alter the six-step learning record's self-check

  Scenario: CONTRIB-003 — Choose sharing deliberately after private preparation
    Given saving, submission and editorial acceptance are separate private steps
    When the learner records an intended attribution and member-only audience
    Then the notebook identifies this as an unsubmitted plan
    And cancelling the plan keeps the private draft
    And the worked example distinguishes withdrawing sharing from removing the private source
    And no button in this local practice creates a real sharing permission

  Scenario: CONTRIB-004 — Recover evidence or writing without inventing permission
    Given source facts or reuse rights are missing, or saving is unconfirmed
    When the learner continues the workflow
    Then they ask for the missing evidence or replace it with original invented material
    And they inspect an uncertain application receipt before replaying an action
    And a failed browser save keeps the local draft editable and downloadable
